    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d315-a2">

                <pb facs="0550" n="488" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg488"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure No. 2 in No. 737.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Rear-Admiral Reynolds
                        to Mr. Bingham</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Flagship Tennessee</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Yokohama,
                                Japan</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1877-06-22"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 22,
                    1877</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Captain Young informs me that he has heard
                    from good authority that the depth of water at this anchorage is diminishing
                    from the throwing overboard of ashes by steamships frequenting Yokohama.</p>
                <p>This is another matter for harbor regulations to take cognizance of and for a
                    harbor-master to enforce attention to. Ashes, as well as other <hi
                        rendition="#italic">débris</hi>, are not allowed to be thrown overboard in
                    harbors, but scows are provided in which they are to be dumped and taken away
                    for discharge at the place indicated by the authorities.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. REYNOLDS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
